{"document_id":"cir-linoleic-acid-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Linoleic Acid — CIR safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/facids042019finalrep.pdf","published_year":2019,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the Safety Assessment of Fatty Acids & Fatty Acid Salts the CIR Expert Panel concluded the assessed fatty acids, including Linoleic Acid, are safe in the present practices of use and concentration when formulated to be non-irritating and non-sensitising. Linoleic Acid is also FDA GRAS as a food substance. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Safety Assessment of Fatty Acids & Fatty Acid Salts as Used in Cosmetics (CIR, 2019).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Safety Assessment of Fatty Acids & Fatty Acid Salts as Used in Cosmetics. 2019.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["linoleic-acid"],"ingredient_names":["Linoleic Acid"],"inci_names":["Linoleic Acid"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record