{"document_id":"reg-alpha-arbutin-sccs-v1","title":"Alpha-Arbutin — EU SCCS regulatory factual card","source":"EU SCCS","source_family":"SCCS","source_url":"https://health.ec.europa.eu/system/files/2023-02/sccs_o_264.pdf","published_year":2023,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: CIR has not published an alpha-arbutin cosmetic assessment; the EU SCCS final opinion (2023) considered alpha-arbutin safe at up to 2% in face cream and 0.5% in body lotion, provided hydroquinone content is kept as low as possible (arbutin can convert to hydroquinone). Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"SCCS Opinion on the safety of alpha-arbutin and beta-arbutin (2023).","citation_text":"Scientific Committee on Consumer Safety (SCCS). Opinion on the safety of alpha-arbutin and beta-arbutin in cosmetic products. 2023.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["alpha-arbutin"],"ingredient_names":["Alpha-Arbutin"],"inci_names":["Alpha-Arbutin"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record (approval_state and routine_selection_allowed in the knowledge-base database), not by any evidence card."}
{"document_id":"reg-piroctone-olamine-eu-v1","title":"Piroctone Olamine — EU regulatory factual card","source":"EU Cosmetics Regulation","source_family":"EU-regulation","source_url":"https://cosmileeurope.eu/inci/detail/11818/piroctone-olamine/","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: Piroctone Olamine is permitted as a preservative in the EU (Annex V), with reported limits around 1.0% in rinse-off and 0.5% in leave-on products; it is not classified as CMR in the EU and is reported as non-mutagenic/non-sensitising at standard use levels. A reviewer should confirm current Annex limits. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"EU Cosmetics Regulation preservative annex status for Piroctone Olamine.","citation_text":"EU Cosmetics Regulation (Annex V preservative) status for Piroctone Olamine.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm current annex limits before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm annex limits","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["piroctone-olamine"],"ingredient_names":["Piroctone Olamine"],"inci_names":["Piroctone Olamine"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record (approval_state and routine_selection_allowed in the knowledge-base database), not by any evidence card."}
{"document_id":"reg-titanium-dioxide-sccs-fda-v1","title":"Titanium Dioxide — SCCS / FDA regulatory factual card","source":"EU SCCS / US FDA","source_family":"SCCS","source_url":"https://health.ec.europa.eu/publications/titanium-dioxide-tio2-used-cosmetic-products-lead-exposure-inhalation_en","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: Titanium Dioxide is a UV filter regulated primarily outside CIR. EU SCCS opinions consider dermally-applied TiO2 (including certain coated nano grades) safe as a UV filter for skin, but not for applications leading to inhalation exposure; genotoxicity concerns exist for some oral grades. In the US, TiO2 is an FDA OTC sunscreen active. A reviewer should confirm current limits. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"EU SCCS opinions on Titanium Dioxide; US FDA OTC sunscreen monograph status.","citation_text":"EU SCCS opinions on Titanium Dioxide in cosmetics; US FDA OTC sunscreen active status.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm current status/limits before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["titanium-dioxide"],"ingredient_names":["Titanium Dioxide"],"inci_names":["Titanium Dioxide"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record (approval_state and routine_selection_allowed in the knowledge-base database), not by any evidence card."}
{"document_id":"reg-tranexamic-acid-status-v1","title":"Tranexamic Acid — regulatory status factual card","source":"Regulatory status summary","source_family":"regulatory-status","source_url":"https://cosmileeurope.eu/","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: neither CIR nor EU SCCS has published a dedicated cosmetic safety assessment for Tranexamic Acid; it is permitted in EU cosmetics and has a substantial pharmaceutical/topical safety literature (topical use commonly studied at ~3-5%). This card records the absence of a dedicated cosmetic panel opinion, not a safety conclusion. Re-checked 2026-09-23: still no CIR or SCCS cosmetic assessment located. Peer-reviewed literature context (not a panel opinion) is linked separately in the corpus: a 2018 systematic review and meta-analysis (PMID 30533427) and a 2017 randomised topical study (PMCID PMC5574746). Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"Absence of dedicated CIR/SCCS cosmetic assessment; EU-permitted; topical pharmaceutical literature.","citation_text":"Regulatory status summary for Tranexamic Acid in cosmetics (no dedicated CIR/SCCS opinion located).","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must establish an appropriate source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual status paraphrase with attribution; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_status_no_dedicated_assessment","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer to source a dedicated assessment","verified_at":"2026-09-23","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["tranexamic-acid"],"ingredient_names":["Tranexamic Acid"],"inci_names":["Tranexamic Acid"],"previous_verified_at":"2026-07-27","recheck_log":[{"date":"2026-09-23","checked":["CIR findings listing","web search for CIR/SCCS tranexamic acid assessments"],"outcome":"no dedicated assessment located; status unchanged"}],"supporting_literature_source_ids":["journal-zhang-tranexamic-meta-analysis-2018","journal-tranexamic-melasma-study-2017"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record (approval_state and routine_selection_allowed in the knowledge-base database), not by any evidence card."}
